Description: a click on the line after the last file of a panel took that line for a file (an index past the list), and dragging from there below the panel crashed mc
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/commit/abbd9d59159fd01c7ae79b80626660f7b28acb67
 and https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/commit/130d0f043508ffc0a16c638a91c8dde8eac1b0a0 (15.02.2025, after 4.8.33)
Bug: https://github.com/MidnightCommander/mc/issues/4651
Why: mc 4.8.33 died with SIGSEGV after a press on the line below the last file of a
 panel that is not full and a drag down out of the panel (each event below it moved
 the cursor further past the list). panel_mouse_is_on_item() returns "after the
 last file" for that line, move_down() keeps the cursor in the list. With
 mouse-sgr-ncurses.patch the mouse works with TERM=xterm, so this is reached there too.

--- src/filemanager/panel.c.orig
+++ src/filemanager/panel.c
@@ -2195,8 +2195,14 @@ move_down (WPanel *panel)
 {
     int items;
 
-    if (panel->dir.len == 0 || panel->current + 1 == panel->dir.len)
+    if (panel->dir.len == 0)
+        return;
+
+    if (panel->current >= panel->dir.len - 1)
+    {
+        panel->current = panel->dir.len - 1;
         return;
+    }
 
     unselect_item (panel);
     panel->current++;
@@ -4062,7 +4068,7 @@ panel_mouse_is_on_item (const WPanel *panel, int y, int x)
     y += panel->top + lines * col;
 
     /* are we below or in the next column of last file? */
-    if (y > panel->dir.len)
+    if (y >= panel->dir.len)
         return MOUSE_AFTER_LAST_FILE;
 
     /* we are on item of the file file; return an index to select a file */
